Practical philosophy

    - … entry to practical philosophy … the cosmic safehold,
      … key … the question, ‘To what end?’
        \ to warrant these claims and this metaphor, their explication:
    - hardly could … contemplate the prospect of entering the safehold without asking that question,
      nor make headway in the philosophy without … an answer [in the context of the safehold]
        \ to warrant these claims re (cQ) the question and (cA) its answer:
\ to warrant (cQ):
    | [the scale|scope of] the safehold makes remote and obscure the ultimate end,
      which in turn presses|urges the question, making it a must-ask as claimed
\ to warrant (cA):
    | in the prospect of a valid answer (ground)
            \ So specifying, what is crucial herein, that in response to the question
            \ a ground is being sought.
        : re `prospect of a (valid) answer.+(ground).+`
          e.g. `^*' \(1\) mere supposition.+there.+could.+be a.+${1}.+reason.+viz. ${2}` @
          ._/02.wrong_rhetoric/wrong_rhetoric.README.brec
        | … find
            | value at stake + method of answering
                : re `(value) at stake` see `^*⇒ the prospect of.+the ${same}.+`s @
                  ._/02.wrong_rhetoric/wrong_rhetoric.README.brec
